On 2006-12-13, Janis Papanagnou <Janis_Papanagnou@hotmail.com> wrote:
> I became aware that, despite a couple of wizard ascensions in the past, I
> never #invoked the amulet (the same with other classes; I mostly forget
> that feature during the game). Will the portals, say if I connect from
> Asmodeus to Sokoban, be placed anywhere in Sokoban? Any suggestions where
> it is especially advantageous to place portals?

The Eye doesn't actually _place_ portals; that is, #invoking the eye 
doesn't mean that you can then go from that point to some other point
again. It just lets you teleport to a "random" location in a branch of
your choice. (Random on the dungeon level that you end up on, but the
level itself is the explored level closest numerically to yours. 
Usually you are coming from below and that means Mines' End or the
bottom of Sokoban; if you are going down, it means the Valley.)

Think of it as like controlled levelport, except controlled branchport.

